WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.801
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:04.637
Thank you for watching.
Thank you for being here.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.873
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.742
Well, guys, this weekend,
President Biden went after

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:12.612
big social-media platforms
like Facebook

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:16.983
for not doing enough to stop the
spread of COVID misinformation.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.651
Yeah.
Our country has gone from

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.653
"The only thing we have
to fear is fear itself"

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.256
to "Please don't take
medical advice from a meme."

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.124
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:27.326
Seriously, you know there's
a problem with Facebook

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:29.562
when you can find more honest
information on Tinder.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.931
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:34.533
Yeah, Biden doesn't want
Facebook to prevent young people

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:36.635
from getting vaccinated.

00:00:36.635 --> 00:00:38.170
Everyone under 30
heard and was like,

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.472
"That is so cute, but literally
none of us use Facebook.

00:00:40.472 --> 00:00:41.808
But that is so..."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:44.210
"Aww."

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.446
Yep, Biden and his
administration are busy.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:49.115
In fact, they're now reversing
a Trump-era rule

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.718
that made showerheads
have more water flow.

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.619
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:55.989
In response, Trump spent the day
inciting a riot

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.490
in the plumbing section
of a Home Depot.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.026
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.861
Speaking of Trump,
check out what the authors

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.696
of a new book said
about the recent interview

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.265
with the former president.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:07.500
-At one point
in the 2 1/2-hour sitdown

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.302
with the book's authors
at Mar-A-Lago,

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.503
Mr. Trump suggested
that if George Washington

00:01:11.503 --> 00:01:14.206
came back from the dead
and chose Abraham Lincoln

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:17.210
as his vice president,
it would have been very hard,

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:19.379
he says, for them to beat him.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:24.917
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:27.086
-If George Washington
came back from the dead

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:30.356
and chose Lincoln
as his running mate.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.292
Does Trump think
Abe Lincoln's still alive?

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:36.129
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:38.097
Well, guys, the Olympics
are almost here,

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:40.600
and the athletes
in the Olympic village

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.769
are sleeping on beds
made of cardboard.

00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:45.805
And some people think
that they're meant

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:47.840
to discourage any intimacy.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.442
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.810
That's nice.
You finally reach

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.146
your Olympic dreams and have
to sleep on an Amazon box.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.080
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.550
That's right, a bed designed
to discourage sex,

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.586
or as it's also known,
an air mattress.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:04.390
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.991
Yeah.
That's right.

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:07.993
'Cause of COVID,
organizers want to make sure

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:10.863
every athlete is as celibate
as a badminton player.

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:14.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.370
Oh, we're gonna get letters
from the badminton people.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.905
[ Laughter ]
[ Cymbals crash ]

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:20.707
Yeah, everyone's
been talking about these beds,

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.675
so a gymnast from Ireland
put them to the test

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.410
in a viral video that he posted.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.945
This is great.
Check this out.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.280
-The beds are meant
to be anti-sex.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.384
They're made out of cardboard,
yes, but apparently,

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:34.087
they're meant to break
at any sudden movements.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.623
It's fake.
Fake news!

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:40.059
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.928
-Yeah, it works fine
as long as you have the body

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:43.696
of a 70-pound Irish gymnast.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:47.333
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:50.269
So you're completely safe as
long as you have sex like this.

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:54.106
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:58.244
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.679
-Jumpin'.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.780
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:02.916
-Here's some good advice.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.216
Yesterday,
during his weekly address,

00:03:04.216 --> 00:03:07.753
Pope Francis urged people
to learn how to take a break

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:10.356
and turn off their phones.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.691
Then the Pope ended his address
by saying, "That's my sermon.

00:03:12.691 --> 00:03:14.794
Be sure to smash that
like button and subscribe."

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.428
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.428 --> 00:03:19.165
Yeah, the Pope said to look
closely at "The Last Supper"

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:21.434
and notice how everyone left
their phones in a pile

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:27.006
at the end of the table.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.342
Jesus was like, "Peter, Matthew,
give up the phone, please."

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.576
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:33.012
"We're not gonna do this again,
hence the title."

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:36.048
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:38.151
-Come on!
[ Applause ]

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:42.689
-"What kind of supper
you think this is?"

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:45.925
Some entertainment news.
I read that Paramount+

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:49.395
has ordered
a "Grease" prequel series.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:50.729
Yeah.
The movie takes place

00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:53.065
before the original "Grease,"
which means the actors

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:57.136
will only be about 48.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.470
[As John Travolta] "Can't
believe I'm in high school.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.306
I got these
high school problems."

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:02.341
I think I'm going
through puberty, right?"

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:03.609
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:05.044
"I can't believe --
Look at this new issue

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:07.513
of 'AARP Magazine,' right?
It's amazing!"

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:12.251
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:15.288
"Ha! You guys get
your Social Security checks?

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:17.256
This party's
gonna be on point."

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:20.960
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.429
"I love being in high school.
It's unbelievable."

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:24.797
-"I've fallen,
and I can't get up."

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:27.299
-"Oh, my God! There's
Werther's Originals everywhere.

00:04:27.299 --> 00:04:30.636
It's amazing, right?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:31.871
[ Normal voice ]
Hey, get this.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:34.006
Over the weekend,
there was a lot of debate online

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:36.308
about the lyrics
to Bruce Springsteen's song

00:04:36.308 --> 00:04:37.944
"Thunder Road."

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:41.414
Some fans think he says,
"Mary's dress sways."

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:45.084
But the rest say it's,
"Mary's dress waves."

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:46.386
Let's hear it.

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:48.855
♪ The screen door slams ♪

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:52.458
♪ Mary's dress sways ♪

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.360
-Yeah, interesting.
Not really sure,

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.496
but we actually have someone
on the phone right now

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:59.531
who can clear it up.
Bruce, are you there?

00:04:59.531 --> 00:05:01.033
-Yeah.
Hey, Jimmy.

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:03.669
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:04.971
-Thank you for being here.
Now, I don't know

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:06.505
if you've heard about this,
but people online

00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:09.108
were having trouble
understanding your song.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:11.110
-Oh, yeah, I heard about that.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:14.480
[ Indiscernible ]

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.981
-Right, right.
Well, I imagine a lot

00:05:15.981 --> 00:05:17.450
of your fans
have been reaching out

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:20.152
and asking
if it's "sways" or "waves."

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:21.220
-Right.
[ Indiscernible ]

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:24.222
-...sways or waves...
[ Indiscernible ]

00:05:24.222 --> 00:05:26.459
...wave runner wave wave.

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:28.827
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.827 --> 00:05:30.996
-Thank you so much for agreeing
to come on the show

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:32.732
and clear things up
once and for all.

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:35.034
Whenever you're ready,
go for it.

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:36.936
-Two, three...

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:39.238
♪ Screen door slams ♪

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:41.707
♪ Mary's dress waaay ♪

00:05:41.707 --> 00:05:43.642
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.642 --> 00:05:49.248
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:50.549
-Thank you so much
for clearing it up.

00:05:50.549 --> 00:05:52.752
Bruce Springsteen, everybody.

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:54.987
-Yeah...
[ Indiscernible ] ...Jimmy.

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:58.391
[ Applause ]

00:05:58.391 --> 00:06:00.626
-It's "sways."
Sure.

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.161
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:03.962
Some business news.
I saw that grocery stores

00:06:03.962 --> 00:06:07.099
are now selling frozen
Chuck E. Cheese pizzas.

00:06:07.099 --> 00:06:08.901
[ Audience groans ]

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:10.869
And this is fun.
The pizza is also being used

00:06:10.869 --> 00:06:12.938
to make the cardboard beds
in the Olympic village.

00:06:12.938 --> 00:06:14.073
-Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:17.310
Isn't that amazing?
-Recycle.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.212
-I read about a man in Florida
who was arrested

00:06:20.212 --> 00:06:24.583
after crashing a stolen car
through an airport fence

00:06:24.583 --> 00:06:26.519
and boarding
a Coast Guard plane.

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:28.087
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:30.056
I mean, I'm not surprised.
It happened in Florida.

00:06:30.056 --> 00:06:31.324
I bet --
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:34.093
I bet we could plug in any three
random words or phrases,

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:36.929
and it would link to an actual
Florida news story.

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:37.963
Let's try it.
It's time for

00:06:37.963 --> 00:06:39.298
"Florida News Roulette."
Here we go.

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:40.299
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:44.570
-♪ Florida News Roulette, yeah ♪

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.839
-Now here's how it works.
The computer will generate

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:48.641
three random words,
and we'll see if there's

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:51.711
a Florida news story
based on those words.

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:53.713 line:0%
Let's get our first three
right now.

00:06:53.713 --> 00:06:56.382 line:0%
[ Beeping ]

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:59.719 line:0%
Candles, bear mace --
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:03.522 line:0%
Candles, bear mace,
and Bath &amp; Body Works.

00:07:03.522 --> 00:07:05.057 line:0%
Bear mace?
-Bear mace.

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:08.160 line:0%
-What's the difference between
bear mace and regular mace?

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:12.564 line:0%
-About $3.50.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:12.564 --> 00:07:13.966 line:0%
-Not sure how those
could make a news story,

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:16.568 line:0%
but, hey, in Florida, who knows?
Let's take a look.

00:07:16.568 --> 00:07:18.637
-Oh, South Florida.
The search is on tonight

00:07:18.637 --> 00:07:21.907
for a man who police say
used bear mace to steal candles

00:07:21.907 --> 00:07:23.508
from Bath &amp; Body Works.

00:07:23.508 --> 00:07:27.746
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:27.746 --> 00:07:31.550
-Wow.
[ Applause ]

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.586
All right, let's give it
another spin here.

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:34.587 line:0%
Here we go.
Let's try.

00:07:34.587 --> 00:07:36.889 line:0%
[ Beeping ]

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:40.726 line:0%
Alligator,
miniature golf, cocktail lounge.

00:07:40.726 --> 00:07:43.762 line:0%
Alligator, miniature golf,
cocktail lounge.

00:07:43.762 --> 00:07:44.997 line:0%
I couldn't even imagine
what this could be.

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:46.198 line:0%
Let's see.

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:48.200
-A Florida man is in jail
after police officers

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:51.003
spotted him trying
to throw a live alligator

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:54.073
onto the roof of
a beachside cocktail lounge.

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:57.509
Police say the 32-year-old man
told officers he stole the gator

00:07:57.509 --> 00:08:00.746
from its pen at a miniature golf
course and was, quote,

00:08:00.746 --> 00:08:02.914
"Teaching it a lesson."
-Yeah, that's right.

00:08:02.914 --> 00:08:05.284
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:07.386
That's right, man.
Taught him a lesson.

00:08:07.386 --> 00:08:08.654
-Showed him.
-Absolutely.

00:08:08.654 --> 00:08:11.357
Showed him, man.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:12.492
-"I'll show you!"

00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:13.925
-He was teaching the alligator
a lesson.

00:08:13.925 --> 00:08:15.794
-The alligator was rude.
-That's right. Absolutely.

00:08:15.794 --> 00:08:18.730
-I'm gonna throw you on top --
-But he was trying to...

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:20.399
-Yeah, he was trying.

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:22.334
Alligator didn't
learn his lesson.

00:08:22.334 --> 00:08:24.203
Let's try one more time.
Here we go.

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:25.371
What have we got?

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:27.873 line:0%
[ Beeping ]

00:08:27.873 --> 00:08:31.143 line:0%
Everglades,
emergency landing, taco.

00:08:31.143 --> 00:08:32.244 line:0%
-Taco.
-All right.

00:08:32.244 --> 00:08:33.545 line:0%
Let's see what happens.

00:08:33.545 --> 00:08:35.681
-A couple of guys had to make
an emergency landing

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:37.949
in their plane
in Collier county last week.

00:08:37.949 --> 00:08:41.220
They survived and told officials
they were flying across

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.455
the Everglades on a taco run.

00:08:43.455 --> 00:08:44.390
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:48.461
-Big deal.
Needed some tacos.

00:08:48.461 --> 00:08:51.497
And, finally, I saw that
there is a Swiss mountain

00:08:51.497 --> 00:08:55.868
for sale on eBay for $235,000.

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:58.404
Sounds like a bargain, but the
shipping costs are a fortune.

